From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:57:28 -0000
Subject: [PATCH] AP: reject vendor commands without a driver context

Removing an owner interface can disable a first-BSS borrower while
retaining its control socket. Its drv_priv is then NULL, but the VENDOR
command still reaches the nl80211 callback, which dereferences that
private context. An explicit DISABLE exposes the same path.

Reject vendor commands in hostapd_drv_vendor_cmd() when drv_priv is
NULL, so VENDOR returns failure on the disabled BSS. Keep live-driver
dispatch and its return value unchanged. This guards the shared wrapper
used by this command; other disabled-BSS command paths need a separate
audit.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/ap/ap_drv_ops.h | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/ap_drv_ops.h b/src/ap/ap_drv_ops.h
index 34f7fb77ce53..b7715930fef7 100644
--- a/src/ap/ap_drv_ops.h
+++ b/src/ap/ap_drv_ops.h
@@ -390,7 +390,8 @@ static inline int hostapd_drv_vendor_cmd(struct hostapd_data *hapd,
 					 enum nested_attr nested_attr_flag,
 					 struct wpabuf *buf)
 {
-	if (hapd->driver == NULL || hapd->driver->vendor_cmd == NULL)
+	if (hapd->driver == NULL || hapd->drv_priv == NULL ||
+	    hapd->driver->vendor_cmd == NULL)
 		return -1;
 	return hapd->driver->vendor_cmd(hapd->drv_priv, vendor_id, subcmd, data,
 					data_len, nested_attr_flag, buf);
